  <h2
    class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.4vw,1.875rem)] font-medium text-fg leading-tight mb-6 max-w-3xl"
  >
    How a run works
  </h2>

  <p class="text-[19px] leading-[1.65] text-fg max-w-3xl mb-10">
    A run is an outer loop driven by an upstream caller. Inside VLAPilot, a
    ReAct runner orchestrates two VLMs &mdash; a planner that decides what to
    do next, and a verifier that watches each step. The runner mediates every
    interaction with the VLA backend, which lives in a separate child process
    and owns all hardware control.
  </p>

